module System

### The quotient and remainder of a single Möller-Granlund 2-by-1 word division.
record WordQuoRem
    q: U64
    r: U64

### A zero-initialized value of type `T` — every field/element set to zero (a null pointer for raw
### pointer fields). The buildtime footprint primitive behind the SoA collections: `SplitList`/
### `SplitItems` start from `blank[T]()` and fill their columns. Gated on `T obeys Splittable` — a
### trivially-destructible, blittable footprint — so the zeroed instance is ALWAYS a valid `T` that owns
### nothing needing teardown. This is why the gate is ENFORCED, not advisory: a non-Splittable `T` with a
### managed field would get an uninitialized lifecycle field (dangling handle → UAF/double-free on read or
### destroy), so `blank` must not exist for it. Splittable is exactly the set where zero-bits is sound.
### :returns: A `T` with every byte zero.
common routine T.blank() -> T
needs T obeys Splittable
    return LLVM::zeroed[T]()

### The hollow `T`: every bit zero. That is `0`, `false`, an empty handle, a collection with no memory, or a
### choice's first member, and for an entity a new entity whose member variables are all zero. Every type has it,
### and the builder makes it. It is `dangerous`: the zero value can break what the type promises (a `Text` with no
### data, an empty `Retained` that is used), so it is called inside `danger`. Every `destruct` leaves a hollow
### value alone. `Addr.hollow()` (the address 0) is its own routine and is not `dangerous`. Test a handle with
### `is_hollow()`, which the nine handle types (`Retained`, `Tracked`, `Guarded`, `Witnessed`, `Roamed`, `Watched`,
### `Hijacked`, `Viewing`, `Modifying`) and `Addr` have.
### :returns: The `T` whose bits are all zero.
@innate
common dangerous routine T.hollow() -> T

### Executes `stop`.
### :throws: May throw {UserTerminationError}.
@crash_only
failable routine stop()
    throw UserTerminationError()

### Checks that `expr` holds, and crashes when it does not.
### :param expr: The condition that must hold.
### :throws: {VerificationFailedError} when `expr` is false.
@crash_only
failable routine verify(expr: Bool)
    if not expr
        throw VerificationFailedError()
    return

### Executes `breach`.
### :throws: May throw {LogicBreachedError}.
@crash_only
failable routine breach()
    throw LogicBreachedError()

### Sets the exit status the program ends with when `start` returns, 0 (success) until something sets it. The last
### call wins: it is one atomic value, so any thread may set it, but a thread still running when `start` returns may
### or may not get its call in. A crash still exits with its own status (82), whatever was set.
### :param code: The exit status.
routine set_exit_code(code: S32)
    C::rf_set_exit_code(code)
    return

### Möller-Granlund reciprocal of a normalized `d`, delegated to the arch-gated C primitive
### `rf_reciprocal_word` (returns 0 on x86-64/MSVC where the divide is hardware; the real M-G
### reciprocal on arm64/wasm). Hoist it: compute once per divisor, reuse across every `div2by1`
### by that `d` — that reuse is what makes M-G win on arm64 (see div_ab_bench).
### :returns: the reciprocal `v` feeding `div2by1` (meaningful only on the M-G targets).
@inline
routine reciprocal_word(d: U64) -> U64
    danger
        return C::rf_reciprocal_word(d: d)

### Möller-Granlund 2-by-1 division `(u1:u0) / d` (NORMALIZED `d`, `u1 < d`) with the precomputed
### reciprocal `v = reciprocal_word(d)`. Delegates to the arch-gated C `rf_udivrem_128_64_pre`:
### hardware `divq` / `_udiv128` on x86-64/MSVC (ignoring `v`), multiply-only M-G on arm64/wasm.
### :returns: the quotient `q` and remainder `r` of `(u1:u0) / d`.
@inline
routine div2by1(u1: U64, u0: U64, d: U64, v: U64) -> WordQuoRem
    var scratch: U64 = 0
    danger
        var q = C::rf_udivrem_128_64_pre(hi: u1, lo: u0, d: d, v: v, rem: scratch.hijack())
        return WordQuoRem(q: q, r: scratch)

routine knuth_divide[LIMBS](
    a: Hijacked[Items[U64, LIMBS]],
    b: Hijacked[Items[U64, LIMBS]],
    rem: Hijacked[Items[U64, LIMBS]],
) -> Items[U64, LIMBS]
needs U64 LIMBS
    var nl = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[U64, S64](LIMBS)
    var q = Items[U64, LIMBS]()
    danger
        var qp = q.hijack()

        # significant limb count of the divisor (highest non-zero limb + 1)
        var n = nl
        until LLVM::signed_le(a: n, b: 1)
            or LLVM::int_ne(
                a: LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    b,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 1)),
                ),
                b: 0,
            )
            n = LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 1)

        # ---- Single-limb divisor: normalized long division via multiply-only div2by1 ----
        # Normalize d0 so its MSB is set (div2by1's precondition); shift the dividend limbs on
        # the fly by the same amount, then denormalize the final remainder by shifting it back.
        if LLVM::signed_le(a: n, b: 1)
            var d0 = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](b, 0)
            var sh1 = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[U64, S64](LLVM::leading_zeros(d0))
            var sh1u = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](sh1)
            var sh1inv = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: 64, b: sh1))
            var pos1 = LLVM::signed_gt(a: sh1, b: 0)
            var dn = LLVM::shift_left(d0, sh1u)
            var vrec1 = reciprocal_word(dn)
            # initial normalized remainder = the bits shifted out past the top limb (< dn, so u1 < d holds)
            var r = if pos1 then LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    a,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: nl, b: 1)),
                ),
                sh1inv,
            ) else 0
            var i = LLVM::sub(a: nl, b: 1)
            until LLVM::signed_lt(a: i, b: 0)
                var ahi = LLVM::shift_left(
                    LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                        a,
                        LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](i),
                    ),
                    sh1u,
                )
                var alo = if LLVM::signed_gt(a: i, b: 0)
                    and pos1 then LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
                    LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                        a,
                        LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: i, b: 1)),
                    ),
                    sh1inv,
                ) else 0
                var dr = div2by1(u1: r, u0: LLVM::bit_or(a: ahi, b: alo), d: dn, v: vrec1)
                LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    qp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](i),
                    dr.q,
                )
                r = dr.r
                i = LLVM::sub(a: i, b: 1)
            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                rem,
                0,
                LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(r, sh1u),
            )
            var z = 1
            until LLVM::signed_ge(a: z, b: nl)
                LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    rem,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](z),
                    0,
                )
                z = LLVM::add(a: z, b: 1)
            return q

        # significant limb count of the dividend
        var mlen = nl
        until LLVM::signed_le(a: mlen, b: 1)
            or LLVM::int_ne(
                a: LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    a,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: mlen, b: 1)),
                ),
                b: 0,
            )
            mlen = LLVM::sub(a: mlen, b: 1)

        # Dividend shorter than divisor → quotient 0, remainder = dividend.
        if LLVM::signed_lt(a: mlen, b: n)
            var z2 = 0
            until LLVM::signed_ge(a: z2, b: nl)
                LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    rem,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](z2),
                    LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                        a,
                        LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](z2),
                    ),
                )
                z2 = LLVM::add(a: z2, b: 1)
            return q
        var m = LLVM::sub(a: mlen, b: n)

        # ---- D1: normalize so the divisor's top limb has its MSB set ----
        var vtop = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
            b,
            LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 1)),
        )
        var s = 0
        until LLVM::int_ne(a: LLVM::bit_and(a: vtop, b: LLVM::shift_left(1, 63)), b: 0)
            vtop = LLVM::shift_left(vtop, 1)
            s = LLVM::add(a: s, b: 1)
        var su = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](s)
        var su_inv = LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: 64, b: s))

        # vn = b << s  (n limbs)
        var vn = Items[U64, LIMBS]()
        var vnp = vn.hijack()
        var vi = LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 1)
        until LLVM::signed_lt(a: vi, b: 0)
            var hi = LLVM::shift_left(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](b, LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](vi)),
                su,
            )
            var lo = if LLVM::signed_gt(a: vi, b: 0)
                and LLVM::signed_gt(a: s, b: 0) then LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    b,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: vi, b: 1)),
                ),
                su_inv,
            ) else 0
            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                vnp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](vi),
                LLVM::bit_or(a: hi, b: lo),
            )
            vi = LLVM::sub(a: vi, b: 1)

        # un = a << s  (mlen+1 limbs; the top limb lives in `un_hi`)
        var un = Items[U64, LIMBS]()
        var unp = un.hijack()
        var un_hi = if LLVM::signed_gt(a: s, b: 0) then LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
            LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                a,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: mlen, b: 1)),
            ),
            su_inv,
        ) else 0
        var ui = LLVM::sub(a: mlen, b: 1)
        until LLVM::signed_lt(a: ui, b: 0)
            var uhi = LLVM::shift_left(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](a, LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ui)),
                su,
            )
            var ulo = if LLVM::signed_gt(a: ui, b: 0)
                and LLVM::signed_gt(a: s, b: 0) then LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    a,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: ui, b: 1)),
                ),
                su_inv,
            ) else 0
            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                unp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ui),
                LLVM::bit_or(a: uhi, b: ulo),
            )
            ui = LLVM::sub(a: ui, b: 1)

        var vn1 = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
            vnp,
            LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 1)),
        )
        var vn2 = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
            vnp,
            LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: n, b: 2)),
        )
        # vn1 is the normalized top divisor limb (MSB set by D1), invariant across the whole
        # quotient-digit loop, so its Möller-Granlund reciprocal is computed exactly once here.
        var vrec = reciprocal_word(vn1)

        # ---- D2..D7: main loop over quotient limbs, high to low ----
        var j = m
        until LLVM::signed_lt(a: j, b: 0)
            # un_get(j+n) is in un_hi when j+n == mlen, else in the un array
            var un_jn = if LLVM::int_eq(
                a: LLVM::add(a: j, b: n),
                b: mlen,
            ) then un_hi else LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                unp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::add(a: j, b: n)),
            )
            var un_jn1 = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                unp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: LLVM::add(a: j, b: n), b: 1)),
            )

            # D3: estimate qhat, rhat from the top two dividend limbs / top divisor limb.
            # rhat can legitimately reach up to 2*(2^64-1) here, which does NOT fit in a U64.
            # Knuth's correction test only applies "while rhat < 2^64"; once rhat overflows a
            # word the estimate is already final. `rhat` is a U64 so its overflow bit is lost on
            # the `un_jn1 + vn1` add — track it explicitly in `rhat_ok` (true iff rhat < 2^64),
            # else the all-ones-qhat case (un_jn == vn1) silently drops the carry and over-corrects.
            var qhat: U64 = 0
            var rhat: U64 = 0
            var rhat_ok = true
            if LLVM::int_eq(a: un_jn, b: vn1)
                qhat = U64_MAX
                rhat = LLVM::add(a: un_jn1, b: vn1)
                # carry-out of the word add ⇒ rhat >= 2^64 ⇒ skip the correction test entirely.
                rhat_ok = LLVM::unsigned_ge(a: rhat, b: un_jn1)
            else
                var dr = div2by1(u1: un_jn, u0: un_jn1, d: vn1, v: vrec)
                qhat = dr.q
                rhat = dr.r
            # correct qhat: while qhat*vn2 > (rhat:un[j+n-2]) and rhat fits 64 bits
            var un_jn2 = LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                unp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::sub(a: LLVM::add(a: j, b: n), b: 2)),
            )
            var done = not rhat_ok
            until done
                var lhs = LLVM::mul(
                    a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](qhat),
                    b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](vn2),
                )
                var rhs = LLVM::bit_or(
                    a: LLVM::shift_left(LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](rhat), 64),
                    b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](un_jn2),
                )
                if LLVM::unsigned_gt(a: lhs, b: rhs)
                    qhat = LLVM::sub(a: qhat, b: 1)
                    var rnew = LLVM::add(a: rhat, b: vn1)
                    if LLVM::unsigned_lt(a: rnew, b: rhat)
                        done = true
                    else
                        rhat = rnew
                else
                    done = true

            # D4: multiply qhat*vn and subtract from un[j..j+n] (signed S128 borrow `k`)
            var k = LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](0)
            var ii = 0
            until LLVM::signed_ge(a: ii, b: n)
                var p = LLVM::mul(
                    a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](qhat),
                    b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](
                        LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                            vnp,
                            LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ii),
                        ),
                    ),
                )
                var plo = LLVM::int_truncate[U128, U64](p)
                var phi = LLVM::int_truncate[U128, U64](LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(p, 64))
                var idx = LLVM::add(a: ii, b: j)
                var cur = if LLVM::int_eq(
                    a: idx,
                    b: mlen,
                ) then un_hi else LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    unp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](idx),
                )
                var t = LLVM::sub(
                    a: LLVM::sub(a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](cur), b: k),
                    b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](plo),
                )
                var tlo = LLVM::int_truncate[S128, U64](t)
                if LLVM::int_eq(a: idx, b: mlen)
                    un_hi = tlo
                else
                    LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                        unp,
                        LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](idx),
                        tlo,
                    )
                # k = phi - arithmetic_shift_right(t, 64)
                k = LLVM::sub(
                    a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](phi),
                    b: LLVM::shift_right_signed(t, 64),
                )
                ii = LLVM::add(a: ii, b: 1)
            # final top limb: un[j+n] -= k
            var topidx = LLVM::add(a: j, b: n)
            var curtop = if LLVM::int_eq(
                a: topidx,
                b: mlen,
            ) then un_hi else LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                unp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](topidx),
            )
            var ttop = LLVM::sub(a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](curtop), b: k)
            var ttoplo = LLVM::int_truncate[S128, U64](ttop)
            if LLVM::int_eq(a: topidx, b: mlen)
                un_hi = ttoplo
            else
                LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    unp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](topidx),
                    ttoplo,
                )

            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                qp,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](j),
                qhat,
            )

            # D5/D6: if the subtraction went negative, qhat was 1 too big — add the divisor back
            if LLVM::signed_lt(a: ttop, b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, S128](0))
                LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    qp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](j),
                    LLVM::sub(a: qhat, b: 1),
                )
                var carry: U64 = 0
                var ai = 0
                until LLVM::signed_ge(a: ai, b: n)
                    var aidx = LLVM::add(a: ai, b: j)
                    var acur = if LLVM::int_eq(
                        a: aidx,
                        b: mlen,
                    ) then un_hi else LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                        unp,
                        LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](aidx),
                    )
                    var sum = LLVM::add(
                        a: LLVM::add(
                            a: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](acur),
                            b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](
                                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                                    vnp,
                                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ai),
                                ),
                            ),
                        ),
                        b: LLVM::zero_extend[U64, U128](carry),
                    )
                    if LLVM::int_eq(a: aidx, b: mlen)
                        un_hi = LLVM::int_truncate[U128, U64](sum)
                    else
                        LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                            unp,
                            LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](aidx),
                            LLVM::int_truncate[U128, U64](sum),
                        )
                    carry = LLVM::int_truncate[U128, U64](LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(sum, 64))
                    ai = LLVM::add(a: ai, b: 1)
                un_hi = LLVM::add(a: un_hi, b: carry)
            j = LLVM::sub(a: j, b: 1)

        # ---- D8: denormalize the remainder (un >> s), low n limbs ----
        var ri = 0
        until LLVM::signed_ge(a: ri, b: n)
            var rlo = LLVM::shift_right_unsigned(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    unp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ri),
                ),
                su,
            )
            var rhi = if LLVM::signed_gt(a: s, b: 0) then LLVM::shift_left(
                LLVM::load_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                    unp,
                    LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](LLVM::add(a: ri, b: 1)),
                ),
                su_inv,
            ) else 0
            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                rem,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](ri),
                LLVM::bit_or(a: rlo, b: rhi),
            )
            ri = LLVM::add(a: ri, b: 1)
        var rz = n
        until LLVM::signed_ge(a: rz, b: nl)
            LLVM::store_element_ref[Items[U64, LIMBS], U64](
                rem,
                LLVM::reinterpret_bits[S64, U64](rz),
                0,
            )
            rz = LLVM::add(a: rz, b: 1)
    return q
